  "description": "QOSTEA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H82 Ho9 N24 O42 1+,5(C1 H4 O1),N1 O3 1-. From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho5 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho2A (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho3A (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho4A (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho5A (Ho) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.510-5.003 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.10-167.06°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ho9(C8H9N2O)8(μ3-OH)8(μ4-OH)2(NO3)8](NO3)·CH3OH·8H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
